  "sourceNotes": [
    "Hypebeast original by Eddie Eng: published November 6, 2026 at 19:00:33 UTC; current dateModified November 9 at 02:42:01 UTC (November 8 in New York). No inference that this metadata update represents a new project announcement. Names and visual traits of six builds attributed to report. No engine figures recast as in-game performance, purchasable liveries or vehicle stats. Physical-build photographs not reused without a separate verified rights basis.",
    "Grand Rex current venue page 5680 and linked Shotgun event fully readable HTTP200: November 19, 2026, 20:00–00:00 Paris CET/UTC+1, four hours, Infinite room, organiser Iconic Production, Vlad_CKa on stage. Official venue advertises EUR 15.40–22 for France, checked November 8 in every translation. Range is an advertisement, not a guarantee all tiers remain for sale or fees are included. No purchase, registration or claim of reserved seats. Event is not labelled an official Rockstar production. Sortiraparis search content updated November 6 provides secondary context; venue has no publication timestamp, so no new November 8 announcement is fabricated.",
    "PlayStation App support and download help confirm pairing through Settings > Pair Console to App, matching account, Game Library > Purchased > Download to Console, rest-mode internet and storage management. Phone install queue is distinguished from streaming. No GTA VI download requested or claimed available before November 10; access still November 19.",
    "Sony licence help gives the Settings > Users and Accounts > Other > Restore Licenses route and the individual-game option. It states restoration does not affect data. Account, preorder clock and download/access issues are separated; no GTA VI fault reproduced or early-unlock method claimed. No save deletion or factory reset recommended.",
    "Sony current GTA VI product page directly lists Remote Play supported, one player and PS5. Official PC/Mac guide and individual download manuals give host settings, same account, USB controller, 5 Mbps standard/15 Mbps recommended upload and download, installer links and manual pairing. They are client requirements, not native GTA VI PC specifications or measured GTA VI streaming performance.",
    "Mac source discrepancy found: general support includes Big Sur, while the current Mac-specific installer guide starts at Monterey. Published table follows the Mac-specific guide, Monterey through Tahoe, and advises checking current installer requirements. No blanket Big Sur compatibility recommendation."
  ],
